1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,266
Welcome.

2
00:00:01,266 --> 00:00:07,993
This tutorial breaks a biomedical agentic pipeline into the components you can ask a coding agent to build.

3
00:00:07,993 --> 00:00:14,243
We will explain the purpose of each skill, helper, and hook, and show a construction prompt you can adapt.

4
00:00:14,243 --> 00:00:18,882
The workshop SAP and datasets are already supplied.

5
00:00:18,882 --> 00:00:22,194
The full prompts and function guide accompany the video.

6
00:00:23,217 --> 00:00:32,857
Here is the task: compare ABC-201 with placebo on change in HbA1c at Week 24, adjusting for baseline.

7
00:00:32,857 --> 00:00:36,040
The supplied analysis plan defines that question.

8
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:44,314
The subject table contains ten synthetic participants, five in each group, with treatment, baseline, and analysis flags.

9
00:00:44,314 --> 00:00:52,497
Two alternative efficacy files link by subject ID: one stops at Week 12; the other includes Week 24.

10
00:00:52,497 --> 00:01:01,247
The pipeline checks the selected file, then either runs the specified analysis and reviews the result, or stops and explains what is missing.

11
00:01:02,283 --> 00:01:05,932
Begin with a user asking the agent an analysis question.

12
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:13,896
The workflow skill tells the agent how to use SAP extraction, readiness checks, analysis, and review.

13
00:01:13,896 --> 00:01:17,581
A structured contract carries the analysis requirements.

14
00:01:17,581 --> 00:01:26,318
The pre-analysis gate either blocks fitting or allows the specified ANCOVA, and final review checks the result before reporting.

15
00:01:26,318 --> 00:01:30,661
The harness supports the conversation, tool calls, and state.

16
00:01:30,661 --> 00:01:35,339
The agent uses the evidence to answer the user, including follow-up questions.

17
00:01:35,339 --> 00:01:39,089
A separate pre-tool hook checks declared data operations.

18
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:42,793
Start with a goal supplied by the user.

19
00:01:42,793 --> 00:01:52,716
This project checks readiness for a Week 24 HbA1c comparison, then estimates the treatment difference only when quality control allows it.

20
00:01:52,716 --> 00:01:58,863
The first step records that goal, the existing inputs, and the component build order in a project protocol.

21
00:01:59,883 --> 00:02:07,707
The prompt supplies the project goal: build a reusable pipeline from an analysis question and estimand to a reviewed result.

22
00:02:07,707 --> 00:02:12,991
Study-specific settings come from the user’s request and statistical analysis plan.

23
00:02:12,991 --> 00:02:17,720
Ask the agent to record the scope and build order before implementation.

24
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:26,522
The SAP skill describes a procedure for turning the analysis plan into requirements that other components can use.

25
00:02:26,522 --> 00:02:30,298
Each field carries its value and source evidence.

26
00:02:30,298 --> 00:02:35,143
The skill also explains how to expose missing or ambiguous information.

27
00:02:35,143 --> 00:02:38,996
Extraction ends before any data readiness decision.

28
00:02:40,017 --> 00:02:45,972
The skill should explain what information to extract, rather than name a particular study endpoint.

29
00:02:45,972 --> 00:02:51,706
The estimand, population, endpoint, and analysis settings become contract fields.

30
00:02:51,706 --> 00:02:58,150
Their values come from the document, with source evidence and explicit status for missing information.

31
00:02:59,183 --> 00:03:04,417
The extraction helper turns the supplied Markdown excerpt into a JSON contract.

32
00:03:04,417 --> 00:03:12,355
It reads sections, labeled values, dash lists, and the model formula, then attaches evidence to each extracted field.

33
00:03:13,383 --> 00:03:18,527
Ask for a parser that produces the contract fields needed by downstream tools.

34
00:03:18,527 --> 00:03:24,016
The prompt names the concepts to extract, while the supplied plan provides their values.

35
00:03:24,016 --> 00:03:31,413
Section and field helpers keep the extraction procedure clear, and the JSON gives later components a common input.

36
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:38,173
The contract, checking table, result, and manifest form the workflow’s state.

37
00:03:38,173 --> 00:03:41,614
Small utilities load JSON and record time.

38
00:03:41,614 --> 00:03:46,614
The artifact helper describes a file by its resolved path and whether it exists.

39
00:03:46,614 --> 00:03:50,248
These records make a completed workflow easier to inspect.

40
00:03:51,283 --> 00:03:54,700
This request describes reusable state utilities.

41
00:03:54,700 --> 00:04:01,723
They record file locations, timestamps, and structured artifacts for whichever analysis the user selects.

42
00:04:01,723 --> 00:04:07,084
The workflow collects those records with its stage decisions so the result can be inspected.

43
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:11,404
The pre-tool hook checks a proposed data operation.

44
00:04:11,404 --> 00:04:19,136
It collects paths, identifies targets under the protected data directory, and applies operation and shell-pattern rules.

45
00:04:19,136 --> 00:04:22,513
The workflow calls it for declared source-data reads.

46
00:04:22,513 --> 00:04:26,971
Its decision matters only where the caller checks and enforces it.

47
00:04:27,983 --> 00:04:31,799
The hook’s purpose is independent of the analysis endpoint.

48
00:04:31,799 --> 00:04:37,353
The prompt defines its operation event, protected-source policy, and decision output.

49
00:04:37,353 --> 00:04:44,789
Protected paths and operation details are inputs, allowing the same check to be used across analysis projects.

50
00:04:45,817 --> 00:04:52,532
The data readiness skill tells the agent which inputs to supply and how to interpret the checker’s evidence.

51
00:04:52,532 --> 00:04:55,625
It uses the chosen efficacy file throughout.

52
00:04:55,625 --> 00:05:05,457
The demo checker requires endpoint coverage for every FAS subject, which is stricter than the SAP’s missing-record exclusion wording.

53
00:05:06,483 --> 00:05:09,874
The readiness skill should work from the contract’s requirements.

54
00:05:09,874 --> 00:05:16,227
A missing endpoint, required visit, or population variable can prevent the intended analysis.

55
00:05:16,227 --> 00:05:22,348
Ask the skill to explain which requirement failed and how that affects the user’s analysis question.

56
00:05:23,383 --> 00:05:27,534
The deterministic checker turns contract requirements into a table.

57
00:05:27,534 --> 00:05:34,944
It checks columns, subject IDs, treatments, population selection, endpoint records, and subject coverage.

58
00:05:34,944 --> 00:05:38,153
Each row records what was expected and observed.

59
00:05:38,153 --> 00:05:43,230
The wrapper writes that evidence and a summary decision for the analysis stage.

60
00:05:44,283 --> 00:05:49,272
The checker should compare actual data with requirements supplied through the contract.

61
00:05:49,272 --> 00:05:55,251
The prompt uses endpoint, population, timing, and coverage as general terms.

62
00:05:55,251 --> 00:06:02,481
Its table explains each finding, and its summary tells the analysis component whether the required checks passed.

63
00:06:03,550 --> 00:06:07,057
The pre-analysis gate sits inside the analysis helper.

64
00:06:07,057 --> 00:06:12,057
It reads the QC summary and continues only for an ALLOW decision.

65
00:06:12,057 --> 00:06:16,979
Other decisions produce a blocked result before dataset construction or fitting.

66
00:06:16,979 --> 00:06:22,856
In this demo, the gate trusts the supplied summary; it does not rerun the data checks.

67
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:28,640
This gate applies to any analysis tool using the same readiness interface.

68
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:34,478
It reads the QC decision and either permits model work or produces a blocked result.

69
00:06:34,478 --> 00:06:38,730
The endpoint and model settings remain in the analysis contract.

70
00:06:39,783 --> 00:06:43,354
The numerical helper separates data selection from model fitting.

71
00:06:43,354 --> 00:06:50,197
It joins the selected endpoint records to FAS subjects and represents active treatment with an indicator.

72
00:06:50,197 --> 00:06:54,257
The model includes an intercept, treatment, and baseline.

73
00:06:54,257 --> 00:07:00,159
The result records the treatment difference, uncertainty, sample counts, and diagnostics.

74
00:07:01,183 --> 00:07:06,069
ANCOVA remains the defined capability of this helper.

75
00:07:06,069 --> 00:07:13,852
The prompt generalizes the endpoint, population, treatment labels, and baseline variable by taking them from the contract.

76
00:07:13,852 --> 00:07:20,154
The returned estimate and uncertainty describe the requested contrast using the selected model settings.

77
00:07:21,183 --> 00:07:26,533
The ANCOVA skill explains how an agent should use the analysis tool.

78
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:31,468
A thin command-line wrapper loads the chosen inputs and calls the gated helper.

79
00:07:31,468 --> 00:07:39,626
It then records the input paths in the result, so the reader can see which contract, QC summary, and datasets were selected.

80
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:46,231
The skill explains when the ANCOVA capability is appropriate and what it needs.

81
00:07:46,231 --> 00:07:51,734
Its wrapper accepts the selected datasets and contract instead of assuming a fixed study.

82
00:07:51,734 --> 00:07:56,914
It reuses the gated helper and returns structured results that the agent can explain.

83
00:07:57,950 --> 00:08:00,748
The final review checks the recorded outcome.

84
00:08:00,748 --> 00:08:09,176
It compares the gate and execution status, aligns model fields with the contract, and inspects statistical fields and counts.

85
00:08:09,176 --> 00:08:14,434
It also checks declared data-handling flags and can scan supplied report text.

86
00:08:14,434 --> 00:08:17,475
Failed checks produce a failed release decision.

87
00:08:18,517 --> 00:08:22,784
The review request is about consistency with the intended analysis.

88
00:08:22,784 --> 00:08:30,193
It takes the model, variables, and contrast from the contract and applies checks appropriate to the supported method.

89
00:08:30,193 --> 00:08:36,869
A completed result, a correctly blocked run, and an inconsistent outcome receive distinct decisions.

90
00:08:37,917 --> 00:08:41,539
The existing demo can check a report supplied by the user.

91
00:08:41,539 --> 00:08:48,846
It scans the text for a short list of clinical or regulatory claim phrases and adds a finding to the final review.

92
00:08:48,846 --> 00:08:51,449
It does not generate a narrative report.

93
00:08:51,449 --> 00:08:56,526
The scan uses keywords, so it does not interpret negation or context.

94
00:08:57,550 --> 00:09:01,946
The report check uses a documented policy for the analysis context.

95
00:09:01,946 --> 00:09:08,415
The prompt asks for phrase matching and a review finding, with the restricted phrases held in one list.

96
00:09:08,415 --> 00:09:13,003
Optional text can then be checked as part of the final result review.

97
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:18,948
The workflow skill teaches the agent how to handle analysis tasks through conversation.

98
00:09:18,948 --> 00:09:24,515
It connects the user's question with the available skills, tools, and decision rules.

99
00:09:24,515 --> 00:09:31,371
The agent may check readiness, carry out an authorized analysis, or explain an existing blocked result.

100
00:09:31,371 --> 00:09:36,088
The harness supports the conversation, tool calls, and working state.

101
00:09:36,088 --> 00:09:44,954
Deterministic tools perform the checks and calculations, while the agent uses their evidence to decide the next action and answer the user.

102
00:09:45,983 --> 00:09:51,552
Ask the coding agent to create instructions that make this workflow usable in conversation.

103
00:09:51,552 --> 00:09:58,601
The skill defines when to use each component, how to respond to a gate decision, and what evidence to include in the reply.

104
00:09:58,601 --> 00:10:02,737
A Python runner can remain a convenience tool for a complete run.

105
00:10:02,737 --> 00:10:07,634
The workflow skill also guides readiness-only tasks and follow-up questions.

106
00:10:08,683 --> 00:10:13,736
To recap the build: first, define the analysis goal and scope.

107
00:10:13,736 --> 00:10:19,471
Second, build the SAP extraction skill and contract helper.

108
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:23,337
Third, add shared state and source-data protection.

109
00:10:23,337 --> 00:10:27,899
Fourth, implement readiness checks and the pre-analysis gate.

110
00:10:27,899 --> 00:10:33,517
Fifth, build gated ANCOVA and final-result review tools.

111
00:10:33,517 --> 00:10:42,203
Finally, connect these components through a workflow skill, so the agent can carry out requested tasks and explain the evidence in conversation.

112
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:48,923
Start by asking Codex to use the existing biomedical workflow skill to answer the primary efficacy

113
00:10:48,923 --> 00:10:51,125
question in the statistical analysis plan.

114
00:10:51,125 --> 00:10:57,577
The request names the source files, keeps the two dataset choices separate, and asks for a report

115
00:10:57,577 --> 00:10:59,475
supported by the generated artifacts.

116
00:10:59,475 --> 00:11:03,250
Codex begins by reading the workflow skill and the plan.

117
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:11,549
The analysis plan defines the target: change from baseline in HbA1c at Week 24, in the full analysis

118
00:11:11,549 --> 00:11:11,988
set.

119
00:11:11,988 --> 00:11:18,111
The requested model adjusts the treatment comparison for baseline HbA1c. Codex uses these

120
00:11:18,111 --> 00:11:20,938
requirements to guide the data checks.

121
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:28,062
The first dataset contains baseline and Week 12 observations, but no Week 24 endpoint records.

122
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:31,538
All ten participants are missing the required endpoint.

123
00:11:31,538 --> 00:11:35,375
Three quality checks fail, so the workflow returns BLOCK.

124
00:11:35,375 --> 00:11:39,412
No ANCOVA model is fitted for this branch.

125
00:11:39,412 --> 00:11:44,425
Codex explains the missing data before moving to the separate complete dataset.

126
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:49,038
For the complete dataset, all sixteen quality checks pass.

127
00:11:49,038 --> 00:11:55,892
The gate returns ALLOW, and the existing analysis tool fits the specified ANCOVA using all ten

128
00:11:55,892 --> 00:11:58,462
participants, five in each treatment arm.

129
00:11:58,462 --> 00:12:03,975
The conversation shows Codex invoking the workflow command and inspecting its outputs.

130
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:10,965
The command output records the stage decisions: statistical analysis plan extraction passed, data

131
00:12:10,965 --> 00:12:16,562
checks allowed analysis, ANCOVA completed, and the result passed release review.

132
00:12:16,562 --> 00:12:22,638
These decisions are also saved in the workflow manifest alongside the commands and artifact paths.

133
00:12:23,050 --> 00:12:26,488
Codex writes and opens the analysis report.

134
00:12:26,488 --> 00:12:32,668
The comparison table makes the two outcomes explicit: the incomplete branch is blocked with zero

135
00:12:32,668 --> 00:12:37,612
qualifying Week 24 records, while the complete branch includes all ten participants.

136
00:12:37,612 --> 00:12:42,438
The report links back to the source plan, quality checks, and analysis artifacts.

137
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:49,375
The adjusted ABC-201 minus placebo difference is minus zero point six one four.

138
00:12:49,375 --> 00:12:55,455
The ninety-five percent confidence interval runs from minus zero point six nine seven to minus zero

139
00:12:55,455 --> 00:12:56,975
point five three one.

140
00:12:56,975 --> 00:13:03,741
The two-sided p-value is approximately four point nine seven times ten to the minus seven, in this

141
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:04,538
synthetic dataset.

142
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:09,112
The final review hook checks the written report for both branches.

143
00:13:09,112 --> 00:13:14,112
The incomplete branch remains BLOCK, and the completed branch receives PASS.

144
00:13:14,112 --> 00:13:16,262
The source files are unchanged.

145
00:13:16,262 --> 00:13:21,565
The finished workflow connects the analysis request, source requirements, data checks, gated

146
00:13:21,565 --> 00:13:25,100
computation, and a report that cites its evidence.
